		<gameEnder />
		<letterStack>
			<letters>
				<li Class="StandardLetter">
					<def>BadNonUrgent</def>
					<label>Breakdown: heater</label>
					<lookTarget>Thing_Heater396224</lookTarget>
					<disappearAtTick>-1</disappearAtTick>
					<text>One of your machines (heater) has broken down. It won't work until a colonist with the Construction work type goes and fixes it.</text>
				</li>
				<li Class="StandardLetter">
					<def>BadNonUrgent</def>
					<label>Heat wave</label>
					<disappearAtTick>-1</disappearAtTick>
					<text>An unusual heat wave has begun.

Heat waves can kill quickly if people start getting heatstroke. Stay cool by building a cooler or getting deep under a mountain.</text>
				</li>
				<li Class="StandardLetter">
					<def>BadNonUrgent</def>
					<label>Mental break: food binge</label>
					<lookTarget>Thing_Human401479</lookTarget>
					<disappearAtTick>-1</disappearAtTick>
					<text>Remington, Commissar is pigging out on food.

The final straw was: Depressive.</text>
				</li>
				<li Class="StandardLetter">
					<def>Good</def>
					<label>Caravan request</label>
					<lookTarget>@WorldObject_0</lookTarget>
					<disappearAtTick>-1</disappearAtTick>
					<text>A nearby settlement, Poet's Rock, contacts you with a special trade request. They would like to purchase:

  Berries x1300

In return, they offer:

  Steel lightsaber (curved hilt) (superior)

This request expires after: 10 days

If you want to make the trade, send a caravan with the requested supplies. You can review this offer by selecting Poet's Rock on the world map.</text>
				</li>
				<li Class="StandardLetter">
					<def>BadNonUrgent</def>
					<label>Psychic drone</label>
					<disappearAtTick>-1</disappearAtTick>
					<text>Every colonist of the female gender winces in pain!

Some distant engine of hatred is stirring. It is projecting a powerful psychic drone over this entire region, on a frequency that only seems to affect the female gender. For a few days, some people's mood will be quite a bit worse.</text>
				</li>
				<li Class="StandardLetter">
					<def>BadNonUrgent</def>
					<label>Mental break: daze</label>
					<lookTarget>Thing_Human1242742</lookTarget>
					<disappearAtTick>-1</disappearAtTick>
					<text>Grey, Page is wandering around in a psychotic state.

The final straw was: In a moderate amount of pain.</text>
				</li>
				<li Class="StandardLetter">
					<def>BadNonUrgent</def>
					<label>Breakdown: geothermal generator</label>
					<lookTarget>Thing_GeothermalGenerator958782</lookTarget>
					<disappearAtTick>-1</disappearAtTick>
					<text>One of your machines (geothermal generator) has broken down. It won't work until a colonist with the Construction work type goes and fixes it.</text>
				</li>
				<li Class="StandardLetter">
					<def>BadNonUrgent</def>
					<label>Zzztt...</label>
					<lookTarget>(131, 0, 134), Map_0</lookTarget>
					<disappearAtTick>-1</disappearAtTick>
					<text>A fault in an electrical conduit has caused a short circuit.

All 6942 Wd of energy in the connected batteries has been discharged in an electrical explosion.</text>
				</li>
				<li Class="StandardLetter">
					<def>BadNonUrgent</def>
					<label>Disease (infection)</label>
					<lookTarget>Thing_Human1647450</lookTarget>
					<disappearAtTick>-1</disappearAtTick>
					<text>Hector has gotten sick from Infection. The infection is in his left leg.

Ensure you have a medical bed and a doctor. Make sure that Hector gets proper treatment and spends as much time in bed as possible.</text>
				</li>
				<li Class="StandardLetter">
					<def>Good</def>
					<label>Rat self-tamed</label>
					<lookTarget>Thing_Rat1535964</lookTarget>
					<disappearAtTick>-1</disappearAtTick>
					<text>A rat has become tame. It is now designated rat 1.</text>
				</li>
				<li Class="StandardLetter">
					<def>BadNonUrgent</def>
					<label>Mental break: hide in room</label>
					<lookTarget>Thing_Human2728</lookTarget>
					<disappearAtTick>-1</disappearAtTick>
					<text>Seymour, Settler is hiding in his room.

The final straw was: Ugly environment.</text>
				</li>
			</letters>
		</letterStack>
